# Data artifacts are hashed byte-for-byte by data/MANIFEST.sha256 and verified by
# tools/verify_data.py, which reads raw bytes off disk. Git's EOL conversion
# (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) rewrites text blobs to CRLF on checkout, which
# makes every text entry in the manifest fail on a Windows clone even when the
# stored content is bit-identical. Marking the data tree as non-text disables
# that conversion, so these files check out identically on every platform and the
# manifest means the same thing everywhere.
data/** -text
